Why This Is Asked

Tests cross-region DVA design with production-grade guarantees.

Key Concepts
- Exactly-once semantics via per-eventId deduplication and conditional writes
- Schema evolution using a registry and partitioned Parquet sinks
- Late-arrival handling with 24-hour backfill window and idempotent reprocessing
- Observability: CloudWatch metrics, DLQ, and alerting
- Trade-offs: cost, latency, and cross-region consistency

Code Example

```javascript
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const ddb = new AWS.DynamoDB.DocumentClient();

async function saveEvent(event) {
  const params = {
    TableName: process.env.TABLE_NAME,
    Item: {
      deviceId: event.deviceId,
      eventId: event.eventId,
      timestamp: event.timestamp,
      data: event.data
    },
    ConditionExpression: 'attribute_not_exists(eventId)'
  };

  try {
    await ddb.put(params).promise();
  } catch (error) {
    if (error.code !== 'ConditionalCheckFailedException') {
      throw error;
    }
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical end-to-end streaming with enrichment, idempotency, error handling, and observability in a beginner-friendly AWS DVA context.

## Key Concepts
- Kinesis Data Streams, Lambda enrichment, DynamoDB cache
- REST API rate-limiting handling and retries
- Idempotent S3 writes with Parquet partitioning
- DLQ, tracing (X-Ray), and LocalStack testing

## Code Example
```javascript
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const dynamo = new AWS.DynamoDB.DocumentClient();
const s3 = new AWS.S3();

async function enrich(event) {
  const id = event.deviceId + ':' + event.ts;
  let meta = await dynamo.get({TableName:'DeviceMeta', Key:{id}}).promise().then(r=>r.Item?.meta);
  if (!meta) {
    const resp = await fetchMetaFromApi(event.deviceId);
    meta = resp.meta;
    await dynamo.put({TableName:'DeviceMeta', Item:{id, meta}}).promise();
  }
  event.meta = meta;
  return event;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle DynamoDB cold starts or cache stampedes in this flow?
- How would you instrument LocalStack tests to validate retry/backoff and DLQ routing?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical design of a privacy-conscious, end-to-end streaming pipeline that validates, masks, deduplicates, and persists data with observability.

## Key Concepts
- Kinesis Data Streams, Lambda, DynamoDB dedup, S3 Parquet storage, DLQ
- JSON schema validation, field-level masking of PII, correlationId
- Backfill strategy, LocalStack testing, basic observability (CloudWatch, X-Ray)

## Code Example
```javascript
function maskPII(record) {
  const r = {...record};
  if (r.email) r.email = r.email.replace(/[^@]+@/, '***@');
  if (r.phone) r.phone = r.phone.length > 4 ? r.phone.slice(0, 3) + '****' + r.phone.slice(-4) : r.phone;
  if (r.ssn) r.ssn = '***-**-' + r.ssn.slice(-4);
  return r;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the masking logic end-to-end, including replays?
- How would you ensure no PII leaks to DLQ or downstream sinks?
- How would you scale this to higher event rates or additional device classes?

## Why This Is Asked
This question introduces Glue Schema Registry and schema evolution, a common but underrepresented real-world constraint for beginner engineers. It tests practical streaming ingestion, data validation, and basic tracing.

## Key Concepts
- Glue Schema Registry
- Backward-compatible schema
- Data enrichment from DynamoDB
- Parquet on S3 with date partition
- Kinesis Data Streams
- DLQ and observability (X-Ray)
- LocalStack testing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode for the consumer path
async function handleRecord(record){
  const valid = validateWithSchema(registry='Telemetry', version='latest', record);
  if(valid){
    const meta = await dynamo.getItem({deviceId: record.deviceId});
    const enriched = {...record, meta};
    await s3.putParquet(enriched, partitionBy='date');
  } else {
    await dlq.push(record);
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle schema evolution with multiple producers using backward compatibility?
- How would you test end-to-end locally when Glue Schema Registry is not available?
